IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cpp-core-application`
IMPORT `cp6-social-insurance-number`

-- Tests of cp6-social-insurance-number.l4 (sections 98 to 100, lines 2677 to 2698 of the Act file).
-- Every expected date is counted by hand from the calendar; the working is in the comment beside it.

§ `Tests -- the Social Insurance Number`

§§ `Not a provision: has a number already been assigned? (sections 2(1) and 100(2))`

-- Inputs: assigned under the authority of an Act of Parliament; caused to be assigned under an agreement.
#ASSERT `an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `s 100(2) — a number caused to be assigned under an agreement is deemed to have been assigned under this Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 100(2) — a number caused to be assigned under an agreement is deemed to have been assigned under this Act` FALSE)

§§ `Section 98: the prescribed form and manner`

-- Inputs: the form is one the Minister authorizes; the manner is one a regulation prescribes. Both are needed.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 98(1): applying for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

#ASSERT `s 98(1) — subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) — subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` FALSE)
-- Inputs: subsection (1) applies; a number has earlier been assigned.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` FALSE FALSE)
-- 10 March 2026 plus 30 days: 21 days to 31 March, 9 more to 9 April.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 9
-- 31 December 2026 plus 30 days is 30 January 2027.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 30
-- 1 February 2024 (a leap year): 28 days to 29 February, 1 more to 1 March, 1 more to 2 March.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2024 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — an application filed on a day is filed in time` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 4 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(1) — an application filed on a day is filed in time` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 4 10))
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — an application filed on a day is filed in time` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- No earliest day is stated (fork C6-F9): a day before the application for the division is not late.
#ASSERT `s 98(1) — an application filed on a day is filed in time` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `Section 98(2): reaching eighteen and working in pensionable employment`

-- Inputs: contract of service; holding an office; the employment is pensionable; so employed on or after reaching eighteen; the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan; subsection 4(2) treats it as employment in another province.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Section 4(1)(a): in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan Part III's provisions about employees in pensionable employment do not apply ...
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- ... unless section 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province (employment by Her Majesty in right of Canada, say).
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Section 2(2): the first day of the month after the month of the eighteenth birthday.
-- 15 March 2000: eighteen on 15 March 2018, treated as reached on 1 April 2018.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` (YMD 2000 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2018 4 1
-- 1 March 2000: the birthday is the first of the month and the month after is still April.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` (YMD 2000 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2018 4 1
-- 31 December 2000: eighteen on 31 December 2018, treated as reached on 1 January 2019.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` (YMD 2000 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2019 1 1
-- 29 February 2004: the core takes the birthday in 2022 as 28 February (its fork F2), so 1 March 2022.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` (YMD 2004 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 1
-- The later of reaching eighteen (1 April 2018) and becoming employed.
#ASSERT `the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2017 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2018 4 1
#ASSERT `the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2019 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2019 8 20
#ASSERT `the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2018 4 1) EQUALS YMD 2018 4 1
-- Inputs: subsection (2) applies; a number has earlier been assigned.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(2) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` FALSE FALSE)
-- Already employed before eighteen: 1 April 2018 plus 30 days is 1 May 2018 (April has 30 days).
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2017 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2018 5 1
-- Employed from 20 August 2019: 11 days to 31 August, 19 more to 19 September 2019.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2019 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2019 9 19
-- Reaches eighteen on 31 December 2018 (treated as 1 January 2019), employed since 1 June 2018: 1 January plus 30 days is 31 January 2019.
#ASSERT `s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2000 12 31) (YMD 2018 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2019 1 31

§§ `Section 98(3): a self-employed individual`

-- Inputs: section 30 requires a return; subsection (1) applies; subsection (2) applies; a number has earlier been assigned.
#ASSERT `s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 98(3) — the last day for applying` (YMD 2027 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 15

§§ `Section 98(4): the Minister assigns the number`

-- Inputs: the individual has applied; a number has earlier been assigned.
#ASSERT `s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 98(4) — a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(4) — a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(4) — a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 98(5) and (6): the employer asks, the employee answers`

-- Inputs: the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment; subsection (2) applies to the employee.
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the employer must require the employee to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(5) — the employer must require the employee to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(5) — the employer must require the employee to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the last day on which the employer must require the employee to inform the employer` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2019 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2019 9 19
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the last day on which the employer must require the employee to inform the employer` (YMD 2000 3 15) (YMD 2017 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2018 5 1
-- A finding: the employer's last day is the employee's own last day under subsection (2) (both say "whichever is the later").
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the last day on which the employer must require the employee to inform the employer` (YMD 2000 12 31) (YMD 2018 6 1) EQUALS `s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` (YMD 2000 12 31) (YMD 2018 6 1)
-- Inputs: the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment; the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan; subsection 4(2) treats it as employment elsewhere.
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Section 4(1)(a): not for employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, unless section 4(2) treats it as employment elsewhere.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 98(6) — the employee must inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 98(6) — the employee must inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` FALSE)
-- Required on 5 February 2026: 23 days to 28 February, 1 more to 1 March, 6 more to 7 March.
#ASSERT `s 98(6) — the last day for the employee to inform the employer` (YMD 2026 2 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 7
#ASSERT `s 98(6) — the last day for the employee to inform the employer` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

§§ `Section 99(1): how the application is signed`

-- Inputs: signed in own hand; unable to sign own name; attested by a mark; number of witnesses; names and signatures shown.
#ASSERT `s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE
-- Two witnesses are enough and three are not too many (fork C6-F11); one is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 3 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE)
-- A person able to sign cannot use a mark instead.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE 2 TRUE)
-- A person unable to sign who makes no mark has not attested.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 2 TRUE)

§§ `Section 99(2): telling the Minister a new name`

-- Inputs: a number has been assigned; already informed another authority; the day the change takes effect; employed in pensionable employment that day; the day later employed; the first day section 33 requires payment.
-- Without a number there is no duty.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
-- Already told another authority empowered to receive it: no duty.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
-- (a) employed that day: 1 June 2026 plus 60 days: 29 days to 30 June, 31 more to 31 July.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2026 7 31
-- (a) governs even if a later event comes.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 9 15)) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 15)) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2026 7 31
-- (b) not employed that day, later becomes employed on 15 September 2026: 15 days to 30 September, 31 to 31 October, 14 more to 14 November.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 9 15)) NOTHING EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2026 11 14
-- (b) required to pay on self-employed earnings from 15 June 2027: 15 days to 30 June, 31 to 31 July, 14 more to 14 August.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2027 6 15)) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2027 8 14
-- Both later events: the earlier governs (fork C6-F8), whichever it is.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 9 15)) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 15)) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2026 11 14
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 12 1)) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 15)) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YMD 2027 8 14
-- Neither later event has come: no time has begun to run.
#ASSERT `s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS `no time for informing the Minister has yet begun to run`

§§ `Section 100(1): agreement with a province`

`cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province A"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS TRUE

`cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province B"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 100(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about assigning Social Insurance Numbers` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 100(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about assigning Social Insurance Numbers` `cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan`)
